# Coach speech (Simplified Chinese, mainland): the review of the player's moves
# (src/coach/review.cpp, review_explain.cpp). Same keys and variants as
# assets/coach/speech/en/review.lang. Subtitle text only: the voice speaks the English line of the
# same key and variant, so each variant translates its English twin. The ".spoken" keys below are
# the English values, copied unchanged (never used).
#
# Placeholders: {your} {your2} / {my} {my2} = a piece with its owner ("你的车", "我的马");
# {t1} {t2} = a piece of either side, owner included; never write 你的 / 我的 in front of them.
# {sq} = a square ("e4"); {move} {best} {reply} = moves ("♘f3"); {line} = a few moves;
# {eval} = "+1.3" or "3步将死"; {m:move} = "2步"; {pts:point} = "3分"; {n} {n2} = plain numbers.
# {text} = name.pattern.* (a mate pattern, said after 叫作 / 这是).
# No space between Chinese and a square, move or digit. Level bands: b1-b2 plain words,
# b3-b4 club vocabulary, b5-b6 terse. Terms: 捉双 (fork), 闪击 (discovered attack), 串击 (skewer),
# 牵制 (pin), 底线 (back rank), 透气孔 (luft), 逃生格 (escape square), 通路兵 (passed pawn),
# 对王 (opposition), 兵的正方形 (square of the pawn), 兵残局 (pawn ending), 双象 (bishop pair),
# 子力 (material), 得子 (to win material), 胜势 (winning position), "{m}步杀" (terse mate in m).

